        {
          "//backrest": "y -6..4: starts at the pan top and stops 10 units up - below the seated eye at 10 and below the grab rail at 6..8, both of which it would otherwise stand in front of. It sits ON the rear 3 units of its own pan, at +X of it, NOT on the end wall. That is forced, not styled: EntityPlayerShapeRenderer.cs:429-431 pins a remote rider's body yaw to the MOUNT's yaw, so both riders always face cabin -X and there is no per-seat facing to be had (an AP's rotationY only reaches seatPos.Yaw, which that renderer ignores). Backs on the two end walls therefore seated one rider correctly and the other facing into his own backrest. Both backs behind both riders = tram seating, the only layout the engine will actually honour. Its front face lands at AP+2, 0.15 units clear of the seated LowerTorso box (worst case, frame 0; the only other keyed channel in sitboatidle is a 1-degree UpperTorso rock TOWARD upright, away from the back). z stays +/-18, not +/-20 like the pan: the sills run y -2..0 at z 18..20 and the backrest would drive straight through them. Ending on the sill's inner face reads as the back being framed by them.",
